      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The database connection is persistently returning `Access denied` errors, so I could not execute verification queries. I've built the SQL entirely from semantic-network evidence (table/column definitions, concept decision guides, and precedent metric SQL). Here is my analysis and final query.\n\n## 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables (investigated):**\n- **LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED** — one row per subject per term in library-reserve scope. Carries `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY` (surrogate/PK), `TERM_CODE`, `SUBJECT_ID`, `SUBJECT_TITLE`, `OFFER_DEPT_CODE`, `OFFER_DEPT_NAME`, `OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME`, `RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME`, `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`. Parent of LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.\n- **LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL** — one row per reserve material per subject offering per term. `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY` (FK), `LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG_KEY`, `LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY`, `TERM_CODE`, `SUBJECT_ID`. Documented as the table \"used to count reserved materials per subject\".\n- **SIS_DEPARTMENT** — department dimension: `DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME`, `SCHOOL_CODE`, `SCHOOL_NAME`, `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING`.\n- **STUDENT_DEPARTMENT** — lighter lookup (code, name, full name, school code/name); no degree-granting flag.\n- **TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED / TIP_DETAIL** — textbook program; `IS_NO_COURSE_MATERIAL` flag, `TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY`.\n- **SUBJECT_OFFERED / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY** — registrar section/subject grain; `SUBJECT_KEY`, `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`.\n- Also retrieved: LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG, LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS, LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR, TIP_MATERIAL, TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS, SIS_SUBJECT_CODE, ACADEMIC_TERMS(_ALL).\n\n## 2. Lineage & Relationships\n`semantic_graph` on LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED confirms: incoming `joins` from **LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL** (child via `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY`), outgoing `joins` to **SIS_DEPARTMENT**, ACADEMIC_TERMS(_ALL), TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_SUMMARY. Concept memberships: `concept_subject_offering_facts`, `concept_course_material_programs`. 28 metrics depend on it.\n\n## 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix**\n\n| Dimension | LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED | TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED | SUBJECT_OFFERED(_SUMMARY) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Granularity | subject/term in **library reserve** scope | subject/term in **textbook** scope | section / subject per term (registrar) |\n| Enrollment | `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` (library snapshot) | `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` (TIP snapshot) | `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`, `SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER` |\n| \"Subject offered key\" | `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY` | `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY` | `SUBJECT_KEY` / `SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY_KEY` |\n| Reserve-material measure | via child LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL | none | none |\n| Dept full name / school name | `OFFER_DEPT_NAME`, `OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME` only | same | same |\n\nEvidence: `concept_subject_offering_facts` comparisons table; column definitions retrieved via `semantic_get`.\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness**\n\n| Atomic requirement | LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED + LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL | TIP_* | SUBJECT_OFFERED* |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| \"reserved library materials\" count | **SUPPORTED** (`COUNT(LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG_KEY)`) | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED |\n| \"ordered by subject offered key\" | **SUPPORTED** (`LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY`) | SUPPORTED (different key) | SUPPORTED (different key) |\n| subject title / term code / offering dept name / responsible faculty | **SUPPORTED** (all four columns present) | SUPPORTED | SUPPORTED |\n| `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` for window MAX | **SUPPORTED** | SUPPORTED | SUPPORTED |\n| dept name / full name / school name + Engineering/Science filter | needs SIS_DEPARTMENT join (**SUPPORTED**) | same | `OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME` inline |\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring**\n- \"reserved library materials\" → lexically anchors to `LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL` (documented: \"Used to count reserved materials per subject\"). Excludes TIP tables.\n- \"subject offered key\" → in the library-reserve population this is `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY` (the documented parent→child key). Precedents dw_3398/dw_4911/dw_3277 use the analogous `SUBJECT_KEY` when the population is SUBJECT_OFFERED; here the population is library subjects, so the library key applies.\n- \"courses that have materials\" → satisfied by the INNER JOIN to LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL (only subjects that actually have reserve material rows survive).\n- \"department name\" vs \"offering department name\" → two distinct requested columns; `OFFER_DEPT_NAME` (library table) is the offering department name, while `DEPARTMENT_NAME`/`DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME`/`SCHOOL_NAME` must come from SIS_DEPARTMENT (the library table has no `DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME`). `column_concept_department_name` confirms DEPARTMENT_NAME and OFFER_DEPT_NAME share the academic value domain, and `concept_department_dimension` decision_guide says school filtering ('Engineering'/'Science') should use SIS_DEPARTMENT.\n- \"Engineering or Science schools\" → `SIS_DEPARTMENT.SCHOOL_NAME IN ('Engineering','Science')` (decision_guide: \"Questions filtering departments by school … Use SIS_DEPARTMENT; it carries SCHOOL_NAME\").\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence**\n- \"current row and next 2 rows ordered by <key>\" MAX-enrollment window: 3 precedents — dw_3398, dw_4911, dw_3277 — all written as `MAX(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) OVER (ORDER BY <key> ROWS BETWEEN CURRENT ROW AND 2 FOLLOWING)` with **no PARTITION BY**.\n- Reserve-material counting via LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED ⋈ LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL: dw_4566, dw_4683, dw_3393, dw_4701.\n- Department-level `HAVING COUNT(...) > N` + school filter: dw_4650, dw_3727, dw_3868.\n- `ROUND(x / NULLIF(y,0), 2)` ratio ordered DESC: dw_1221, dw_4650.\n\n## 4. Business Usage\nLIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED serves library-reserve enrollment/material questions (28 dependent metrics, categories \"Library Reserve and Enrollment/Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\"). SIS_DEPARTMENT is the canonical school/degree-granting filter dimension. LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL is the bridge used for all reserve-count metrics.\n\n## 5. Coverage Checklist\nAll Phase-1 entities investigated: tables LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL, SIS_DEPARTMENT, STUDENT_DEPARTMENT, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, TIP_DETAIL, SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (`semantic_get` + `semantic_graph` query_neighbors/metrics_by_table on LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED); concepts concept_course_material_programs, concept_subject_offering_facts, concept_department_dimension (`semantic_get`); column_concepts enrollment_measures, material_status_key, department_name, subject_id, term_code, master_subject_id (`semantic_get`/search); metrics dw_3398, dw_4911, dw_1221, dw_3356, dw_1689, dw_3868, dw_4701, dw_4566, dw_4683, dw_3277, dw_4650, dw_3727, dw_1973, dw_4640, dw_5103, dw_3393 (`semantic_get`). Remaining Phase-1 hits (facilities/space/IAP/CIP/time-dimension entities) were screened as unrelated to library-reserve/department semantics.\n\n**Note:** `mysql_query` returned `1045 Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'` on every attempt (12+ retries), so empirical verification was impossible; the query is grounded solely in retrieved schema/precedent evidence.\n\n## 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a. Tables/columns:** LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED (subject title, term code, offering dept name, responsible faculty, `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`, `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY`, `OFFER_DEPT_CODE`) ⋈ LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL (reserve count) ⋈ SIS_DEPARTMENT (dept name, full name, school name, school filter).\n\n**6b. Approach:** (1) department-level CTE counting reserve rows with `HAVING COUNT > 20` and `SCHOOL_NAME IN ('Engineering','Science')`; (2) de-duplicated subject-level CTE (INNER JOIN to reserve detail = \"courses that have materials\"; `DISTINCT` on the unique `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY` prevents fan-out from the 1:N reserve join); (3) global `MAX(...) OVER (ORDER BY LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY ROWS BETWEEN CURRENT ROW AND 2 FOLLOWING)` per precedent; (4) `ROUND(total/NULLIF(max_enrolled,0),2)` ordered DESC.\n\n**6c. Reasons:** *Data* — `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY` is the documented unique surrogate, so DISTINCT yields one row per subject and avoids reserve fan-out corrupting the window; SIS_DEPARTMENT is the only candidate carrying both `SCHOOL_NAME` and `DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME`. *Semantic-network* — parent/child `joins` edge LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL→LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED; `concept_department_dimension` decision_guide mandates SIS_DEPARTMENT for school filtering; `column_concept_enrollment_measures` confirms `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` is the library-scope enrollment measure. *Business* — three precedents use the identical unpartitioned 3-row MAX window; dw_1221/dw_4650 establish the `ROUND(...,2)` ratio-DESC convention.\n\n**6d. Tie-breaker:** STUDENT_DEPARTMENT could equally supply `DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME`/`SCHOOL_NAME` (precedents dw_4640/dw_5103 use it), but it lacks the degree-granting flag and is not the guide-recommended school filter; SIS_DEPARTMENT was chosen. If \"courses that have materials\" were instead meant as `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.IS_NO_COURSE_MATERIAL='N'`, an extra TIP join would be needed — the join-match rate between library subjects and TIP subjects would resolve this, but it is unverifiable while the DB is inaccessible.\n\n",
